{number: 140}
{title: I Need Thee Every Hour}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] I need Thee every hour,
[F] Most gracious [C] Lord;
No tender voice like Thine
Can [G7] peace af-[C] ford.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
I [C] need Thee, O I need Thee;
[G7] Every hour I [C] need Thee;
O [F] bless me now, my [C] Savior,
I [G7] come to [C] Thee.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] I need Thee every hour,
[F] Stay Thou near [C] by;
Temptations lose their pow'r
When [G7] Thou art [C] nigh.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] I need Thee every hour,
In [F] joy or [C] pain;
Come quickly and abide,
Or [G7] life is [C] vain.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[C] I need Thee every hour,
Teach [F] me Thy [C] will;
And Thy rich promises
In [G7] me ful-[C] fill.
{end_of_verse}
